==Strategy==
This stage is fairly light on the difficulty, despite the inclusion of some usually difficult enemies.

The startoff is easy, as while there is only one Sir Seal to give money initially, all of the difficult enemies take a long time to spawn. In particular, the only real pusher, Dread Bore, spawns over a minute into the stage, by which point there will have been plenty of time to setup, assuming the base isn't already rushed by that point.

Due to the abundance of [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] and [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth Enemies]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] are especially useful, with the latter stacking both [[Behemoth Slayer]] and [[Massive Damage]] to deal devastating damage to the combined trait enemies, and being able to clean up annoying Zollow corpses with [[Soulstrike]].

The [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies don't need to be meat shielded, so feel free to only bring Zombie targeting ones. Overall though, the lack of enemy spawns on base hit allow for very aggressive play without consequences, so prioritize damage and speed over range or defense.

===Recommended Ubers===
*Zombie Killers: Most of the [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|Iron Legion]], but especially [[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Atlantis Logistix]] for mobility and raw damage, along with [[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]] to control the smaller enemies.
*[[:Category:Cats with Toxic Immunity|Toxic Immunes]]: Also many of the [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|Iron Legion]], [[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|CAT-10 Gigapult]], [[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Deaths Daughter Lunacia]], [[Sarukani (Uber Rare Cat)|Sarukani]].

